# C2-S08 / C2-S09 — the arena trial and the arena memorial.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2307–2343.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/arena_district.tscn. Losing never hard-fails.

~ enter
Vex: Ironhold! Here's a face you haven't seen before! Fresh off the road, still got all its teeth!
Elara: Hit the one that's trying to hit you.
Kaelen: Thanks.
Elara: I'm support.
[if ch2_seraphina_met] Seraphina: His left shoulder drops before he swings.
[if ch2_seraphina_met] Kaelen: Now that's support.
[if ch2_seraphina_met] Elara: I liked you better before the armour.

# Between rounds, after the first win.
~ memorial
Kaelen: The names carved on that wall. Some of them are flickering.
Seraphina: The arena started as defender training. People wanted danger with a bell.
Kaelen: What does that mean?
Seraphina: Outside the walls, danger comes whenever it likes. In here, we ring first.
Kaelen: These names keep changing.
Seraphina: That's why I keep paper copies.
set ch2_arena_memorial_seen

~ victory
Vex: And the crowd goes— well, the crowd goes somewhere! Come back tomorrow, fighter!

~ defeat
Vex: Down he goes! Up he gets, I hope. Nobody leaves my arena dead, that's the one rule.

~ again
Vex: Another round? Press {ui_accept} to fight again, or {ui_cancel} to go back to the city.

~ again_after_loss
Vex: Bad luck, fighter. Every loss teaches you something. Press {ui_accept} to try again, or {ui_cancel} to leave.
